From: apklayer <noreply@apklayer.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENT: berberis.sigaction_stub.<package> / BERBERIS_SIGACTION_STUB=1 gives one app the fatal-signal stub as the old action again

A guess, labelled as one: PGR with the 0025 translator (rt_sigaction reported the fatal-signal stub as the old action of SIGSEGV/SIGILL/SIGBUS/SIGFPE)
lived longer in three runs than with 0028 (SIG_DFL). Later runs with and without this switch crashed in the same range (switch off: 74, 92, 40 s; on:
44, 61 s), so it changed nothing measurable. Kept as a switch because it is off by default and costs nothing; Gecko, Breakpad and Go need SIG_DFL
(0028). The property name must fit in 64 characters: berberis.sigaction_stub.<package> does not for a long package (use the environment variable).
Module libberberis_arm64.

diff --git a/guest_os_primitives/guest_signal_handling.cc b/guest_os_primitives/guest_signal_handling.cc
--- a/guest_os_primitives/guest_signal_handling.cc
+++ b/guest_os_primitives/guest_signal_handling.cc
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #include <cstddef>
 #include <memory>
 #include <mutex>
+#include <string>
 // region digitalis
 #include <android/log.h>
 // endregion
@@ -387,6 +388,27 @@
 
 const GuestAddr kFatalGuestHandlerStub = ToGuestAddr(&kFatalGuestHandlerStub);
 
+namespace {
+
+// apklayer patch (EXPERIMENT, a guess): berberis.sigaction_stub.<package>=1 (BERBERIS_SIGACTION_STUB=1 in the environment) makes one app's
+// rt_sigaction report the fatal-signal stub as the old action of SIGSEGV/SIGILL/SIGBUS/SIGFPE again, as before 0028. PGR ran longer with that
+// (2 of 3 runs without a crash report in 130-165 s, against 38-39 s with SIG_DFL; too few runs to trust): the switch makes the comparison one
+// property, not a translator swap. Off by default: Gecko, Breakpad and Go need SIG_DFL (a chained handler that jumps to the stub spins).
+bool ReportFatalStubAsOldAction() {
+  static const bool value = [] {
+    if (const char* package = GetAppPackageName(); package != nullptr) {
+      std::string prop = std::string("berberis.sigaction_stub.") + package;
+      ConfigStr app("BERBERIS_SIGACTION_STUB", prop.c_str());
+      if (app.get() != nullptr) return app.get()[0] == '1';
+    }
+    ConfigStr var("BERBERIS_SIGACTION_STUB", "berberis.sigaction_stub");
+    return var.get() != nullptr && var.get()[0] == '1';
+  }();
+  return value;
+}
+
+}  // namespace
+
 }  // namespace
 
 void InitGuestSignalHandling() {
@@ -669,7 +691,7 @@
   // apklayer patch: the fatal-signal stub claims SIGSEGV/SIGILL/SIGBUS/SIGFPE, but it is the address of a host variable, not guest code: a crash
   // handler that chains to the old action (Gecko's, Breakpad's) would jump to it and loop in berberis_HandleNoExec for ever. The guest has
   // not installed a handler: report SIG_DFL, as the kernel does.
-  if (changed && old_act && old_act->guest_sa_sigaction == kFatalGuestHandlerStub) {
+  if (changed && old_act && old_act->guest_sa_sigaction == kFatalGuestHandlerStub && !ReportFatalStubAsOldAction()) {
     old_act->guest_sa_sigaction = Guest_SIG_DFL;
     old_act->sa_flags = 0;
     old_act->sa_mask = {};
